  "id": "precedence-effect",
  "term": "precedence effect",
  "definition": "In cognition, the precedence effect here refers to global precedence: the usual tendency to process the overall, whole pattern in a visual scene before its smaller local parts. It describes a bias toward global information during global-local visual processing.",
